# Regenerable data — the pipeline in CLAUDE.md rebuilds all of it.
# Raw PDFs alone are 26 GB; nothing here belongs in a git repo.
data/*

# …except data/interim, which carries the extraction outputs. Rebuilding
# facts_*.jsonl needs an A100 that the local machines do not have, so those
# files are effectively irreplaceable and belong in the repo. The parsed
# full text does NOT: fulltext*.jsonl is 2.0 GB over seven files, every one
# of them past GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit, and it is re-fetchable
# from arXiv. It ships through the data bundle release instead.
!data/interim/
data/interim/fulltext*.jsonl
run/
reports/*
!reports/chat.html
dist/
vscode-extension/*.vsix
.bak/
.cache/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
nohup.out
bin/
data/meili/
src/*.egg-info/
build/
report_roadmap.md

# API keys for the eval harnesses (scripts/eval) — never committed
.env

# Internal working notes — not part of the published project.
todo.md

# Parsed arXiv HTML, one file per edition (icml.html_extract) — same reason as
# fulltext*.jsonl above: large, and rebuildable from data/raw/html by --reparse.
data/interim/html/
# Rule-found benchmark mentions (icml.bench_mentions): 200 MB, rebuilt from
# data/interim/html in ~45 min, no model involved.
data/interim/mentions/

# Maintainers' working notes, agent instructions and internal evaluations —
# kept locally, never published (removed from the repository 2026-10-07).
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
/.claude/
/docs/platform-survey-*.md
/docs/similar-projects-survey.md
/docs/figure-verification-prior-work.md
/docs/blue-ocean-eval-*.md
/docs/harness-comparison-*.md
/scripts/eval/
